      "message": "The problem this solves is that all-framework-module-impl compiles against module_current, which forces all it\u0027s dependencies to also compile against module_current, otherwise you will get the following error:\n\n```\nerror: frameworks/base/api/Android.bp:89:1: module \"all-framework-module-impl\" variant \"android_common\" (created by module \"frameworks-base-api\"): compiles against module API, but dependency \"framework-virtualiz\nation.impl\" is compiling against private API. In order to fix this, consider adjusting sdk_version: OR platform_apis: property of the source or target module so that target module is built with the same or small\ner API set when compared to the source.\n```\n\nThis allows future-updatable modules to keep compiling against hidden APIs while they transitioning to becoming an updatable module.\n\nI\u0027ve also update the commit message to mention this",
